      ":question/id": "b00836e9-614b-58d1-9355-6c47b3edf3b5",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Find the exact solution of the equation $7^{x+5}=20.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we take $\\log_{7}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7^{x+5}&=20\\\\\\log_{7}(7^{x+5})&=\\log_{7}(20)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx+5=\\log_{7}(20).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5&=\\log_{7}(20)\\\\x&=\\log_{7}(20)-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{7}(20)-5$.",
